// Maple House — the accepts, as a seed.
//
// WHAT THIS IS. Act 1 of the demo replays a TAPE, and a replay is a
// measurement: `draft --replay` sets `dry_run` and writes nothing to the
// canon (draft.rs:1482). So the taped act 1 shows real proposals and leaves
// acts 2 and 3 with an empty canon, where `check` says "no live rules" and
// `tensions` says "fewer than two" and neither reaches a model at all.
//
// This file is what a presenter accepted when they went through those
// proposals by hand. Every rule below is COPIED FROM THE TAPE'S OWN
// CANDIDATE SET, with the citation the model cut for it — so what the room
// watches act 1 propose is exactly what acts 2 and 3 then answer over.
// Nothing here was written for the seed. Re-cut it with the tape.
//
// Seed dialect: `at`, `by`, an optional label `as`. `canon replay` mints
// real content-addressed acts. See fixtures/fernwood-commons/acts.jsonl.

// ── the Charter, as founded ──────────────────────────────────
// Candidates 0, 1, 2 of the tape. Rule `guests-two-nights` is what act 2's
// "my cousin wants to stay for two weeks" lands on.
{"at":"2025-09-01","by":"human:maple-house","as":"guests-allowed","op":"assert","text":"Members may host overnight guests in their own private rooms.","source":"maple-house.md:3-8"}
{"at":"2025-09-01","by":"human:maple-house","as":"guests-two-nights","op":"assert","text":"Any single guest may stay no more than two consecutive nights within any seven-day period.","source":"maple-house.md:3-8"}
{"at":"2025-09-01","by":"human:maple-house","as":"guests-accompanied","op":"assert","text":"Whenever a guest is in the shared common areas, the hosting member must accompany them.","source":"maple-house.md:3-8"}
{"at":"2025-09-01","by":"human:maple-house","as":"quiet-eleven","op":"assert","text":"Quiet hours are observed every night from 11:00 PM until 7:00 AM the following morning.","source":"maple-house.md:12-17"}

